(ns sensor-sim
  "kami-sensor-sim -- camera / lidar / IMU / contact sensor synth.

   Restored from the deleted `kami-sensor-sim` Rust crate
   (`kotoba-lang/kami-engine`, removed in PR #82 \"Remove Rust workspace\")
   as zero-dependency, portable CLJC (JVM / SCI / ClojureScript / GraalWM /
   kotoba-WASM), per ADR-2607010930 (`com-junkawasaki/root`).

   Original crate scope (`lib.rs`, ADR-2605261800): analytic-CPU
   implementations of all four `isaacsim.sensors.{Camera, LidarRtx,
   IMUSensor, ContactSensor}`-compat sensor types; the crate's own planned
   R1.2+/R1.6 WebGPU-compute acceleration (WGSL raster + ray-query against a
   scene BVH) was never implemented before deletion, so there is nothing
   further to port for that scope -- only the CPU analytic models below.

   Submodules (one per original `src/*.rs` module):

   | Namespace          | Restored from | Purpose |
   |---------------------|----------------|---------|
   | `sensor-sim.math`   | (glam usage, extracted) | vec3 / mat3 / affine3 / quat helpers shared by every sensor. |
   | `sensor-sim.camera` | `camera.rs`    | Pinhole `Camera`: intrinsics from HFOV, extrinsics via `look-at`, 3D-point projection, depth-image rasterization. |
   | `sensor-sim.lidar`  | `lidar.rs`     | Analytic ray-cast `Lidar` (VLP-16 / toy intrinsics) against a `Scene` of `Primitive`s (ground-plane / sphere / AABB). |
   | `sensor-sim.imu`    | `imu.rs`       | Body-frame `Imu`: finite-difference proper acceleration + rotated angular velocity, physics-engine-agnostic (takes world-frame link state as input). |
   | `sensor-sim.contact`| `contact.rs`   | Sphere-approximated `ContactSensor` (`sample` nearest, `sample-all` every overlap) vs the same `Primitive`/`Scene` types as `sensor-sim.lidar`. |

   Excluded: the four `tests/*_on_genesis.rs` cross-crate integration tests
   (`camera_on_genesis.rs`, `contact_on_genesis.rs`, `imu_on_genesis.rs`,
   `lidar_on_genesis.rs`) drove a `kami_genesis::IsaacWorld` physics
   articulation (via `kami_articulated::parse_urdf` + an embedded cartpole
   URDF fixture) to prove each sensor reads real physics-engine link state
   correctly. `kami-genesis` (the physics engine) has never been restored as
   a `kotoba-lang` repo, and `kami-articulated` (the URDF parser) is
   currently an empty mid-restoration placeholder -- see
   `kotoba-lang/kami-shugyo`'s README, which duck-typed both of these same
   gaps rather than waiting on them. Faithfully porting these four
   integration tests would require reimplementing a full rigid-body physics
   engine as a side effect of restoring a *sensor* crate, which is out of
   scope here; every *sensor-side* assertion those tests made (projected
   depth tracks distance, contact penetration grows, lidar range tracks
   distance, IMU reads +g at rest / proper accel under force) is already
   covered by the inline `#[test]` units ported 1:1 below, which construct
   world-frame states directly instead of deriving them from a driven
   articulation."
  (:require [sensor-sim.math :as math]
            [sensor-sim.camera :as camera]
            [sensor-sim.lidar :as lidar]
            [sensor-sim.imu :as imu]
            [sensor-sim.contact :as contact]))

(def adr "ADR-2605261800")
(def phase "R1.1-pinhole-camera+R1.x-lidar-imu-contact")
(def kami-name "kami-sensor-sim")
(def nv-compat-target "isaacsim.sensors")
(def supported-sensors ["camera" "lidar" "imu" "contact"])
